Lolly patch 0005: no MCP browser bridge.

Why: upstream starts a WebSocket client (src/session/bridge-client.ts) that
lets a local MCP server drive the editor. Inside Lolly the frame runs
untrusted songs and must talk only to the page that holds it, so the bridge
is never started and drops out of the build (the editor build refuses a
bundle that still opens a WebSocket). The file itself is left as upstream
wrote it, so an upstream change to it never breaks this patch.

Applied by scripts/vendor-rondocode.ts with git apply --directory=packages/rondo/upstream.

